## The Case for Doing Less

Forty designs, and not one of them asked for a skill you do not already have. That was the point.

Simple was never the compromise option. It was the design choice that got dismissed while everyone assumed impressive had to mean complicated, and 2026's entire trend direction is proof that assumption was wrong. A toothpick, a bobby pin, a sponge, that's the complete kit behind most of this list, and every one of these looks holds up next to a design that took an hour and a fine detail brush.

Pick one. Not the one that photographs best in a grid of forty, the one that matches what your Tuesday actually looks like. <strong>Simple nail designs</strong> reward exactly that kind of restraint, one deliberate colour, one clean line, one finish you will not get tired of by Thursday. That is not a lower bar. It is a different one, and among <strong>simple nail designs</strong> specifically, it was the smarter choice the entire time.
